<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Prepare for visiting {{ data['prison-name'] }}</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">All visitors over 16 years old must show <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/management-of-security-at-visits-policy-framework-open-estate/acceptable-forms-of-identification-id-when-visiting-a-prison-in-england-and-wales-annex-a" class="govuk-link">acceptable forms of ID</a> to enter the prison.</p>  
<p class="govuk-body">Visitors should arrive 45 minutes before the visit starts.</p>  
<p class="govuk-body">You can read more about visits at <a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foston-hall-prison" class="govuk-link">{{ data['prison-name'] }}</a>. This includes information on getting to the prison and visiting facilities.</p>  

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What to expect when visiting a prison</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">Visitors will be searched before entering the prison visiting room.</p>  
<p class="govuk-body">Prison staff may check visitors’ pockets, pat them down and ask them to go through a metal detector. Dogs may also be used to detect illegal substances.</p> 

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Help with the cost of prison visits</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">You may be able to <a href="https://www.gov.uk/help-with-prison-visits" class="govuk-link">get help with the cost of prison visits</a> if you’re getting certain benefits or have a health certificate.</p>